  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "The origin of a positive integer is determined by iteratively summing its digits until only a single digit remains.\n\nFor instance, to compute the origin of 129129129,\n\n\nThe sum of digits of 129129129 is 1+2+9=121+2+9 = 121+2+9=12.\nThe sum of digits of 121212 is 1+2=31+2 = 31+2=3.\n\nSo, the origin of 129129129 is 333.\nGiven a positive integer NNN, calculate the sum of the origin values of every integer from 111 to NNN.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of a single line of input, containing one integer NNN.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the sum of the origin values of integers from 111 to NNN.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤10181 \\leq N \\leq 10^{18}1≤N≤1018"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n5\n12\n1000000000000000000",
        "output": "15\n51\n4999999999999999996",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: In this case the answer is simply 1+2+3+4+5=151+2+3+4+5=151+2+3+4+5=15\nTest case 222: In this case we have to find the sum of origins of every integer from 111 to 121212.\n\n111 through 999 are their own origins.\nThe origin of 101010 is 111, since 1+0=11+0 = 11+0=1.\nThe origin of 111111 is 222, since 1+1=21+1 = 21+1=2.\nThe origin of 121212 is 333, since 1+2=31+2 = 31+2=3.\n\nSo, the answer is 1+2+3+4+5+6+7+8+9+1+2+3=511+2+3+4+5+6+7+8+9+1+2+3 = 511+2+3+4+5+6+7+8+9+1+2+3=51."
      }
    ]
  },
